# Response headers for the site on Cloudflare Pages.
# tools/site/steps/90-cloudflare.py copies this file to the root of dist/.
#
# Syntax and limits (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/):
# at most 100 rules and 2,000 characters per line; one splat (*) per path; a
# request takes the headers of every rule it matches, in file order; a header
# set by two rules is joined with a comma, so a narrower rule first detaches
# ("! Name") what it replaces. Pages does not apply this file to responses
# from Pages Functions (the site has none) or from the assets Worker, which
# sets its own headers on /assets/. The share Worker on /play/* passes on
# the headers Pages gave each response, so these rules hold there too.

/*
  # Cross-origin isolation. The player runs the emulator on threads, which
  # needs SharedArrayBuffer, and browsers only expose that to a page whose
  # document sends COOP and COEP. The headers are on every path because
  # workers and worklets are checked too, and because a document that lacks
  # them cannot open the player in the same browsing context group.
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  # Pages adds "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *" to every asset. Nothing here
  # is meant to be loaded by another origin, and the header would contradict
  # the resource policy above for requests made with CORS.
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin

  # Caching. The pages, the catalogue, the front page's files and
  # /play/config.json keep their names from one deployment to the next, so
  # nothing here may be reused without asking the server first.
  # "max-age=0, must-revalidate" makes the browser keep its copy and
  # revalidate it on every use. Pages sends an ETag for every asset and
  # answers an unchanged one with 304 and no body, so a returning visitor
  # pays one small round trip per file. This is also what Pages sends by
  # default; it is written out so that the policy does not depend on a
  # default. stale-while-revalidate would show one stale mixed version after
  # each deployment. Cloudflare's own edge cache is not governed by this
  # header: Pages keeps assets at the edge until the next deployment replaces
  # them.
  #
  # The zone overrides this for scripts and style sheets: its Browser Cache
  # TTL turns their lifetime into "max-age=14400", four hours, whatever this
  # file says. The front page's /style.css and /js/*.js are served that way.
  # The player's files must never be mixed across builds, so they get
  # addresses that change with their content instead: the /play/b/* rule.
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

  # Security headers. HTTPS only from the first visit on.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Only the site itself may frame its pages (X-Frame-Options for browsers
  # that predate frame-ancestors).
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  # Device features no page of the site uses. Fullscreen, gamepads, audio
  # playback and storage are not listed and keep their defaults.
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), serial=(), usb=()
  # Everything comes from the site's own origin except the visitor
  # statistics: no other third-party scripts, styles, fonts or frames
  # (cross-origin isolation rules most of them out anyway). What the other
  # sources are for:
  #   telemetry.bad.cash  Umami's tracker and session recorder, which
  #                       tools/site/steps/80-telemetry.py adds to every page
  #                       (with crossorigin, as COEP requires); what they send
  #                       goes there under connect-src https:
  #   'wasm-unsafe-eval'  compiling WebAssembly (the emulator; nothing else is evaluated)
  #   'unsafe-inline'     inline scripts and styles in the front page and the docs
  #   blob:, data:        images and downloads the pages build in memory
  #   connect-src https:  the player's loader can fetch a firmware or a game from a URL the visitor types in
  #   connect-src wss:    the multiplayer relay under /net/ on the site's own two host names. Current
  #                       Chrome and Firefox take 'self' to cover a WebSocket to the page's own host;
  #                       older Safari does not, so the hosts are named
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://telemetry.bad.cash; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https: wss://n-ga.ge wss://dev.n-ga.ge data: blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

/play/*
  # The player holds the visitor's saves and takes URLs from the address bar,
  # so it gets the stricter policy: scripts only from files of this site, no
  # inline script. Its page has none; tools/site/steps/90-cloudflare.py fails
  # the build if one appears. The statistics host is allowed as above. Workers (the emulator's threads) and the audio
  # worklet are files of the site as well and need nothing more. connect-src
  # is the same as above: this is the page that opens the relay's WebSocket.
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://telemetry.bad.cash; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https: wss://n-ga.ge wss://dev.n-ga.ge data: blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

/s/*
  # The front page's style sheet and scripts, in a folder named after a hash
  # of them (tools/site/build.py), for the same reason as the player's files
  # below.
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/play/b/*
  # The player's own files: everything of the web build but the page and
  # config.json. tools/site/build.py puts each build in a folder named after
  # a hash of its content, /play/b/<hash>/, and points the page there, so
  # these addresses never change their content and can be kept for good. That
  # also takes them out of reach of the zone's Browser Cache TTL, which
  # rewrites short lifetimes on scripts and styles: a script of the last
  # build kept for hours next to a fresh wasm is what "wasmExports.Dc is not
  # a function" was. tools/web/sitecheck.mjs fails on a player file that is
  # neither here nor revalidated.
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# No Content-Type rule: Pages takes the type from the file extension, and
# .wasm is served as application/wasm (which streaming compilation requires)
# without being told. "wrangler pages dev" shows the same types locally.

# Search engines should list the live site only. The dev site (dev.n-ga.ge,
# which shows the Pages branch "dev") and every *.pages.dev address,
# production's own included, are for looking at, not for finding.
https://dev.n-ga.ge/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
